#. translators: Status of a document, shown in brackets after a language name in the content deletion dialog, as in "German (published)". Lower case, inside a sentence.
msgid "published"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Status of a document, shown in brackets after a language name in the content deletion dialog, as in "German (draft)". Lower case, inside a sentence.
msgid "draft"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Status of a document waiting for review, shown in brackets after a language name in the content deletion dialog. Lower case, inside a sentence.
msgid "pending review"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Status of a document set to publish at a future date, shown in brackets after a language name in the content deletion dialog. Lower case, inside a sentence.
msgid "scheduled"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Status of a document only logged-in editors can see, shown in brackets after a language name in the content deletion dialog. Lower case, inside a sentence.
msgid "private"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Status of a document that was moved to the Trash, shown in brackets after a language name in the content deletion dialog, as in "German (in the Trash)".
msgid "in the Trash"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Joins a list of language names in the content deletion dialog. %1$s: the language names before the last one, already joined by commas, %2$s: the last language name.
#, js-format
msgid "%1$s and %2$s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Separator between names in a list, as in "German, Spanish and French". Keep the trailing space.
msgid ", "
msgstr ""

msgid "Each one comes back with the status it had before."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Sentence added under the question in the content deletion dialog when restoring. %d: how many documents one restore brings back at a time.
#, js-format
msgid "WPML brings back %d at a time — run Restore again for the rest."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the content deletion dialog. %1$s: a list of language names, %2$s: one language name, %3$s: the content type, singular, e.g. "page".
#, js-format
msgid "%1$s stay online. The %2$s %3$s becomes the one the others are translated from, because it is first in your language order — choose a different one."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the content deletion dialog. %1$s: a list of language names, %2$s: one language name, %3$s: the content type, singular, e.g. "page".
#, js-format
msgid "%1$s stay online. The %2$s %3$s becomes the one the others are translated from."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the content deletion dialog. %s: a list of language names.
#, js-format
msgid "%s stay online."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Question at the top of the content deletion dialog when content is being restored from the Trash. %1$s: the content type, singular, e.g. "page", %2$d: how many other documents went to the Trash with it.
#, js-format
msgid "This %1$s went to the Trash with %2$d other. What should come back?"
msgid_plural "This %1$s went to the Trash with %2$d others. What should come back?"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Line at the top of the content deletion dialog naming the document being deleted. %1$s: the language name, %2$s: the title of the document.
#, js-format
msgid "This is the %1$s translation of '%2$s'."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Line at the top of the content deletion dialog naming the document being deleted. %s: the language name.
#, js-format
msgid "This is the %s translation."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Question at the top of the content deletion dialog for a menu. %s: a list of the language names the menu exists in.
#, js-format
msgid "This menu exists in %s. What should happen to them?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Question at the top of the content deletion dialog, used when every translation is published. %1$s: the content type, singular, e.g. "page", %2$d: the number of translations, %3$s: a list of language names.
#, js-format
msgid "This %1$s has %2$d translation — %3$s, all published. What should happen to them?"
msgid_plural "This %1$s has %2$d translations — %3$s, all published. What should happen to them?"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Question at the top of the content deletion dialog. %1$s: the content type, singular, e.g. "page", %2$d: the number of translations, %3$s: a list of language names, each followed by its status in brackets when the statuses differ.
#, js-format
msgid "This %1$s has %2$d translation — %3$s. What should happen to them?"
msgid_plural "This %1$s has %2$d translations — %3$s. What should happen to them?"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the content deletion dialog when restoring. %1$s: the content type, singular, e.g. "page", %2$d: how many other documents went to the Trash with it.
#, js-format
msgid "This %1$s and the %2$d other that went to the Trash with it"
msgid_plural "This %1$s and the %2$d others that went to the Trash with it"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the content deletion dialog when restoring. %s: the content type, singular, e.g. "page".
#, js-format
msgid "Only this %s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the content deletion dialog. %d: how many documents stay in the Trash; the singular form has no number in it.
msgid "The other one stays in the Trash."
msgid_plural "The other %d stay in the Trash."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the content deletion dialog. Verb, imperative; "them" is the translations of the document being deleted.
msgid "Delete them permanently too"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the content deletion dialog. Verb, imperative; "them" is the translations of the document being moved to the Trash.
msgid "Trash them too"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the content deletion dialog. %1$d: the number of documents, %2$s: the content type, plural, e.g. "pages".
#, js-format
msgid "All %1$d %2$s leave the site together."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the content deletion dialog. %1$d: the number of documents, %2$s: the content type, plural, e.g. "pages".
#, js-format
msgid "All %1$d %2$s leave the site together. Restoring any one of them brings back the whole set."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the content deletion dialog. %1$s: the language name, %2$s: the content type, singular, e.g. "page".
#, js-format
msgid "Only this %1$s %2$s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the content deletion dialog. Verb, imperative. %d: the number of translation jobs still running for this content.
#, js-format
msgid "Delete them all permanently and cancel the %d translation job in progress"
msgid_plural "Delete them all permanently and cancel the %d translation jobs in progress"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the content deletion dialog. Verb, imperative. %d: the number of translation jobs still running for this content.
#, js-format
msgid "Trash them all and cancel the %d translation job in progress"
msgid_plural "Trash them all and cancel the %d translation jobs in progress"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

msgid "Stops work already under way. Words already sent are still charged."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Badge on a choice in the content deletion dialog. %s: the number of words already sent for translation, written with thousands separators.
#, js-format
msgid "%s word already charged"
msgid_plural "%s words already charged"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the content deletion dialog. %1$s: the language name, %2$s: the content type, singular, e.g. "page".
#, js-format
msgid "Only the %1$s %2$s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the content deletion dialog. %s: a list of language names.
#, js-format
msgid "%s stay exactly as they are."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the content deletion dialog. %s: the language name of the original document.
#, js-format
msgid "The %s original and all its translations"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the content deletion dialog. %1$d: the number of documents, %2$s: the content type, plural, e.g. "pages".
#, js-format
msgid "All %1$d %2$s are deleted permanently. This is a bigger action than the one you started — we ask every time."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the content deletion dialog. %1$d: the number of documents, %2$s: the content type, plural, e.g. "pages".
#, js-format
msgid "All %1$d %2$s go to the Trash. This is a bigger action than the one you started — we ask every time."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of the checkbox at the bottom of the content deletion dialog. %s: a content type as the settings table names it, e.g. "Pages and posts".
#, js-format
msgid "Do this for %s from now on, and stop asking"
msgstr ""

msgid "Image files on disk are kept when other copies share them."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Note in the content deletion dialog; "This" is the document being deleted, and "it" is that same document.
msgid "This is a duplicate, kept in step with its original. Deleting it permanently removes it for good — duplication does not bring it back."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Note in the content deletion dialog; "This" is the document being moved to the Trash, and "it" is that same document.
msgid "This is a duplicate, kept in step with its original. Saving that original brings it back out of the Trash — delete it permanently to remove it for good."
msgstr ""

